6. SCATTER_RATIO: Quantifies the distribution of inertia between the major and minor axes.
7. ELONGATEDNESS: Represents elongation or stretching of the shape.
8. SCALED_RADIUS_OF_GYRATION: Characterizes the spread of mass in relation to the area.
9. SKEWNESS_ABOUT_MAJOR_AXIS and SKEWNESS_ABOUT_MINOR_AXIS: Describe the asymmetry of the distribution along major and minor axes.
10. KURTOSIS_ABOUT_MAJOR_AXIS and KURTOSIS_ABOUT_MINOR_AXIS: Capture the peakedness of the distribution, indicating irregularities in shape.

These features encompass geometric properties, symmetry, and shape irregularities critical for distinguishing vehicle types. They can effectively guide downstream tasks such as feature transformations and engineering.

